WEBVTT

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:16.616
There it is.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.284
You're going to ride in that?

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.487
Yeah.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.856
You're getting ahead of me, Jin.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:26.326
I'm just catching a lift to
my mom's work, that's all.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.795
I was lucky.

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:33.967
An astronomer, huh?
You know, I'm so jealous.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.035
It's nice, huh?

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.798
Jin...

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.640
Dad!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.477
Well? Starting to get nervous yet?

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:46.312
A little bit.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.015
Everyone feels nervous at first.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:53.720
But once you get into space,
that goes away pretty quickly.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:59.759
Space is great! Especially the beauty
of Earth, when seen from space.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.091
You could say it's life-changing.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.666
I want to show it to you, too.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.668
Dad...

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:11.538
Captain Kamishina, it's almost time!

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:13.907
Yeah, I'll be right there!

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.000
See you on the Moon.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.672
Dad!

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.120
Jin...

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.288
Be careful, okay?

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:32.452
Yeah. Thanks for coming all
the way down here, Kazuki.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.865
Well, off I go.

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.701
Get a good look for me, too.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.362
Sure.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:17.003
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you
for boarding ISDA flight 029 today.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:21.074
We will now begin accelerating.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:24.577
- While taxiing, we will experience a
maximum of 1.6 Gs of acceleration.
- Brother, did your girlfriend come?

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:27.180
- While taxiing, we will experience a
maximum of 1.6 Gs of acceleration.
- No!

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.849
- Please check your seatbelts once again.
- I know. It's Kazuki-kun, right?

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.951
You're not that popular,
after all, Brother.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.086
What?!

00:02:33.086 --> 00:02:36.456
Mom! Brother's picking on me!

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:40.654
Both of you, we're taking off,
so behave yourselves.

00:02:56.609 --> 00:03:00.547
ISDA029, runway entry, hold position.

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:02.215
Advise when ready to taxi.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:03.550
Ready for departure.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.553
ISDA029, cleared for taxi out.

00:03:06.553 --> 00:03:09.386
Runway is clear. Countdown adjusting.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.456
Starting roll.

00:04:11.017 --> 00:04:12.882
I'm off.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:18.958
- Lt's true!
- Oh, yeah, is that right?

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:22.862
Come on, hurry up and eat,
then get going. You'll be late.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.454
Okay!

00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:39.935
And so, I was all alone.

00:04:54.994 --> 00:05:01.000
In my younger days, I lost

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.839
even the reason for this pain

00:05:06.839 --> 00:05:12.578
Crouching over, making excuses

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.775
I must have...

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:23.523
Taking hold of the premonition
I saw at the end of the blue,

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:31.030
riding the wind, I'm off
to where the light shines

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.966
I'll always be with you

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.536
see the sky in front of you

00:05:36.536 --> 00:05:40.939
fly high in a light from the deepest blue

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:48.214
Riding the echo of swirling stars,

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:50.817
I sing out

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:59.486
May my voice reach you

00:06:25.551 --> 00:06:29.756
Today, we have the captain
of ISDA's Lindworm Unit,

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:33.092
Raina Cromwell-san with us in the studio.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:36.596
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:39.899
Let's get right to it. Please tell us
about the current status of Thanatos

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:42.201
and the results of
missile tests you conducted

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:44.570
with your latest model the other day.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:48.741
Right. Thanatos is
stationed in Pluto's old orbit,

00:06:48.741 --> 00:06:51.077
and we have not detected
any new movement.

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:55.515
Then, there's no possibility of
it ever approaching Earth again?

00:06:55.515 --> 00:06:58.017
No, that possibility is not zero.

00:06:58.017 --> 00:07:01.521
In order for ISDA to be
ready for any contingency,

00:07:01.521 --> 00:07:04.557
we are starting up and
implementing D Project.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.692
In our benchmark tests that
we conducted the other day,

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:08.728
we successfully obliterated all asteroids

00:07:08.728 --> 00:07:11.964
within a 15km radius of our new missile.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:17.036
With those results, D Project
is now moving on to phase 3.

00:07:17.036 --> 00:07:19.038
Thank you very much.

00:07:19.038 --> 00:07:22.141
Next, a follow-up on our
report about that serial killer.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:25.941
Last night before dawn, in
Shin-Ogasawara Terminal City...

00:07:30.917 --> 00:07:33.317
Oh, there he is.

00:07:35.121 --> 00:07:37.214
Kamishina Jin-kun?

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:41.994
Have you read this yet?

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:42.995
"Suspicions About His Survival!!"
Have you read this yet?

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:43.791
"Suspicions About His Survival!!"

00:07:48.801 --> 00:07:50.826
Not very friendly, huh?

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:59.645
It's been two years since the
accident. The only survivor,

00:07:59.645 --> 00:08:03.115
the son of the pilot whose error it was,

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:05.618
is apparently not getting
along well with the relatives

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.950
who have taken him in, is that right?

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.825
Please, leave me alone.

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.656
Hey, just a minute!

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:23.293
Well, what's his deal?

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:33.338
That was...

00:08:41.153 --> 00:08:43.356
You're as popular as ever, huh?

00:08:43.356 --> 00:08:45.057
Don't tease me.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:48.794
I'm jealous. I want to
share your good fortune.

00:08:48.794 --> 00:08:53.065
So, next time, you'll appear
in my place, Howling Star?

00:08:53.065 --> 00:08:55.966
I think I'd better pass.

00:08:57.003 --> 00:09:00.495
We'd never fit all the presents in this car.

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.019
Hey, did you see it?
It's on the stands today.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:15.021
- I saw it, I saw it!
- Lt's all about Kamishina, right?

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:17.423
- Seriously?
- Shh, he'll hear us!

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:20.984
No wonder he always seemed gloomy,
ever since he transferred here.

00:09:25.765 --> 00:09:28.029
Aren't you getting off?

00:09:37.376 --> 00:09:39.211
Well, how about it?

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:42.281
How about what?
You can't tell from just this

00:09:42.281 --> 00:09:46.786
whether or not she's the
Communicator for the Album.

00:09:46.786 --> 00:09:50.923
We'll have to catch her, and
study every inch of her body.

00:09:50.923 --> 00:09:53.359
- Good grief.
- What?

00:09:53.359 --> 00:09:57.063
At least take off the lab coat
when we're having tea.

00:09:57.063 --> 00:10:00.066
I don't want to waste any time.

00:10:00.066 --> 00:10:02.626
Contact me if anything else comes up.

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:07.039
Not very friendly, huh?

00:10:07.039 --> 00:10:12.445
I'm treading on thin ice bringing
this information straight to you.

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:14.914
Let go.

00:10:14.914 --> 00:10:16.882
And if I say no?

00:10:51.784 --> 00:10:56.122
I figured this is where you
would be, Professor Nozaki.

00:10:56.122 --> 00:10:59.125
We're conducting a
new Resonance tonight.

00:10:59.125 --> 00:11:01.527
Is that right? I look forward to it.

00:11:01.527 --> 00:11:05.164
Every time I come here, I think,

00:11:05.164 --> 00:11:08.300
there's a reason for
every encounter we have.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:11.470
There's no such thing as
a meaningless encounter.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:16.669
There's no such thing as a
meaningless encounter, huh?

00:11:36.228 --> 00:11:39.165
Amazing!

00:11:39.165 --> 00:11:45.137
Dad... Mom... Ai...

00:11:45.137 --> 00:11:48.197
It's lonesome, being by myself.

00:12:13.332 --> 00:12:16.235
What? Don't tell me you're nervous.

00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:20.005
I-I can't help it. This is
my first time, after all.

00:12:20.005 --> 00:12:22.174
First time, eh?

00:12:22.174 --> 00:12:25.701
Well, you want me to
show you how it's done?

00:12:28.047 --> 00:12:32.006
Kid, even your ears are
turning red! That's so cute!

00:12:33.519 --> 00:12:37.022
You're being vulgar, Akira-chan.

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:39.225
Okay, okay.

00:12:39.225 --> 00:12:41.460
Akira-chan, only answer once.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.087
Okay, okay.

00:13:41.086 --> 00:13:43.452
Commencing Resonance.

00:14:11.684 --> 00:14:16.288
All Resonant and G-10 values
stable and within tolerances.

00:14:16.288 --> 00:14:19.024
Congratulations, Tachibana Kazuki-kun.

00:14:19.024 --> 00:14:21.026
Resonance was successful.

00:14:21.026 --> 00:14:24.230
You are now officially
one of the Dragonauts.

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.132
My...

00:14:27.132 --> 00:14:29.362
My own dragon...

00:14:33.038 --> 00:14:35.174
Hey... c-come on!

00:14:35.174 --> 00:14:37.076
"Come on"?

00:14:37.076 --> 00:14:39.203
Please!

00:14:44.683 --> 00:14:48.020
It's "pretty please," right?

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:51.854
"P-Pretty please."

00:15:05.604 --> 00:15:08.038
"Construction Notice"

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:52.551
Um, is something the matter?

00:15:52.551 --> 00:15:54.280
Uh...

00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:19.174
After him.

00:16:45.304 --> 00:16:47.101
You're a monster...

00:16:53.946 --> 00:16:55.777
Hey...

00:16:59.385 --> 00:17:02.286
Oh, you're still alive.

00:17:03.822 --> 00:17:05.653
Well, now...

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:22.732
Why?

00:17:24.209 --> 00:17:27.474
Why... is this happening to me?

00:17:36.688 --> 00:17:38.553
This is just...

00:17:40.526 --> 00:17:42.357
...like before...

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:38.644
No doubt about it.
That girl is a Communicator.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.921
It's Yonamine.

00:18:42.921 --> 00:18:44.389
The Album has appeared!

00:18:44.389 --> 00:18:47.126
Shin-Ogasawara Terminal City,
redevelopment district,

00:18:47.126 --> 00:18:48.727
Point Alpha-107.

00:18:48.727 --> 00:18:50.395
Commander Sakaki...

00:18:50.395 --> 00:18:54.299
Request Dragonauts deployment.

00:18:54.299 --> 00:18:55.634
All right.

00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:58.967
Please be sure you
catch her. I'm counting on it.

00:19:00.572 --> 00:19:02.597
Commander...

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:10.749
Finding stray dogs is no job
for the Dragonauts. However...

00:19:10.749 --> 00:19:13.650
...the Album is a different matter.

00:20:40.005 --> 00:20:42.107
Young Miss, they appear
to have gotten away...

00:20:42.107 --> 00:20:43.836
I know.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:10.631
Where am I?

00:21:15.307 --> 00:21:20.579
That's right, I was
attacked by that monster.

00:21:20.579 --> 00:21:22.376
And then...

00:21:33.158 --> 00:21:34.989
You're the one from before...

00:21:37.496 --> 00:21:39.396
Who are you?

00:21:42.668 --> 00:21:45.837
I'm Toa.

00:21:45.837 --> 00:21:47.828
Toa...

00:21:49.074 --> 00:21:52.134
Just then, I thought to myself...

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:01.084
...that I wasn't alone.

00:22:07.759 --> 00:22:14.433
The moment our eyes met,

00:22:14.433 --> 00:22:21.206
I felt like the sadness was beginning

00:22:21.206 --> 00:22:27.879
The memories that can't be blotted out

00:22:27.879 --> 00:22:35.115
bind our hearts together, even now

00:22:36.955 --> 00:22:43.795
Though there are as many people

00:22:43.795 --> 00:22:46.798
as there are in these thousands of stars,

00:22:46.798 --> 00:22:50.669
you're the only one that I can see

00:22:50.669 --> 00:22:53.839
Though we may not be able to meet,

00:22:53.839 --> 00:22:56.742
and our wishes might not be granted,

00:22:56.742 --> 00:23:03.048
our growing feelings
are sure to last forever

00:23:03.048 --> 00:23:10.055
If fate tears the two of us apart,

00:23:10.055 --> 00:23:16.895
I believe that just meeting
each other was a miracle

00:23:16.895 --> 00:23:23.502
Look how it flows, like this rain

00:23:23.502 --> 00:23:29.541
I want to let all of my affection fall on you

00:23:29.541 --> 00:23:33.739
Rain of Love

00:23:43.855 --> 00:23:45.757
This is ISDA operator Ryoko.

00:23:45.757 --> 00:23:47.526
- And this is Megumi.
- I'm Saki.

00:23:47.526 --> 00:23:49.594
- There's something I want to check.
- What?

00:23:49.594 --> 00:23:51.963
We're always together, right?
A trio of close-knit operators,

00:23:51.963 --> 00:23:54.533
a squad of g*rls of one
body and mind, right?

00:23:54.533 --> 00:23:56.034
Squad of g*rls of one body and mind?

00:23:56.034 --> 00:23:58.036
I'm as envious as can be, really.

00:23:58.036 --> 00:24:01.139
I-I can't help it, can I?
Sometimes, these things come up!

00:24:01.139 --> 00:24:02.574
What do you mean, "sometimes"?

00:24:02.574 --> 00:24:04.910
- That was mean!
- Oh, the preview, the preview!

00:24:04.910 --> 00:24:07.712
Next time, something
big is going to appear!

00:24:07.712 --> 00:24:09.577
Nicely glossed over!
